  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Anil Kumar Rawat vs State Of Up And 4 Others on 9 May, 2024 Author: Dinesh Pathak Bench: Dinesh Pathak High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad ?Neutral Citation No. - 2024:Ahc:83674 Court No. - 6 Case :- Writ - C No. - 12963 of 2024 Petitioner :- Anil Kumar Rawat Respondent :- State Of Up And 4 Others Counsel for Petitioner :- Sanjeev Kumar Khare Counsel for Respondent :- C.S.C. Hon'ble Dinesh Pathak,J. 1.",
    "facts": "2. Petitioner has invoked the extra-ordinary jurisdiction of this Court under Article 226 of the Constitution of India assailing the order dated 19.03.2024, whereby learned Commissioner (respondent no.2) has reviewed the earlier order dated 31.01.2024. 3. It evince from the record that food license granted to the petitioner under the Food Safety & Standard Act, 2006 (in brevity 'Act, 2006') has been suspended vide order dated 19.12.2022 (Annexure No.4). Having been aggrieved with the said order, petitioner has preferred an appeal. It appears that, at later stage, designated officer under the Act, 2006 has filed a review application dated 06.02.2024. Learned Commissioner, vide order dated 19.03.2024, has allowed the review application and [LEAKAGE_MASK] the order dated 31.01.2024, which is under question before this Court. There is no observation qua issuance of notice to the petitioner and it's service upon him for hearing on review application dated 06.02.2024.",
    "arguments": "5. Learned counsel for the petitioner has advanced two fold submissions; first, no opportunity has been accorded to the petitioner before passing the order dated 19.03.2024 and second, there is no provision in the Act, 2006 for review of the order passed by the authority concerned. 6. Per contra, learned Standing Counsel has vehemently opposed the submission as advanced by learned counsel for the petitioner and supported the order impugned dated 19.03.2024. While confronted with learned Standing Counsel on the point of opportunity of hearing, as submitted by learned counsel for the petitioner, he could not rebut such fact.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "5. Learned counsel for the petitioner has advanced two fold submissions; first, no opportunity has been accorded to the petitioner before passing the order dated 19.03.2024 and second, there is no provision in the Act, 2006 for review of the order passed by the authority concerned. 6. Per contra, learned Standing Counsel has vehemently opposed the submission as advanced by learned counsel for the petitioner and supported the order impugned dated 19.03.2024. While confronted with learned Standing Counsel on the point of opportunity of hearing, as submitted by learned counsel for the petitioner, he could not rebut such fact.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
